tei:div.tei:ab:
October 4: Brahms Op. 119, No. 1, graph;
                    Urlinie of Paisiello’s theme used by
                    Beethoven.

June 13: The latest Handel discoveries in Die Musik shown;
                the piece in C minor as attributed to Bach; hasty run-through of Mendelssohn’s “Spring Song”
                and a piece in B minor.

October 19: Graph of
                the Brahms finished;
                    fingering and performance.

January 18: Observations on Furtwängler’s concert; 
Paganini-Variationen,
new.

October 22: On Beethoven’s First Symphony (Dirk Fock);
                Mass in B minor
                    finished.

March 1: Concerning the Backhaus concert;
Scarlatti, volumes 4 and 5
    examined.

December 18: Op. 32, No. 3, wiederholt; Waltz in A major and D major;
                    Berceuse, especially the
                    beginning.
